OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F319A1786425557
OL,3,CWorld's seas hit hottest July
OL,4,Ctemperature on record, scientists say
OL,6,FThe extreme heat began in May and has
OL,7,Fcontributed to major wildfires,
OL,8,Fprolonged drought and new national
OL,9,Ftemperature records across Europe, as
OL,10,Fwell as thousands of projected heat-
OL,11,Frelated deaths.
OL,13,FGlobally, so far this is the third-
OL,14,Fhottest year, behind 2024 and 2025,
OL,15,Fclimate statistics show. But 2026
OL,16,Fstill has time to catch up.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G2/8
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
