CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F319A1786425557
OL,3,CWorld's seas hit hottest July
OL,4,Ctemperature on record, scientists say
OL,6,FThanks to the combination of
OL,7,Faccelerated human-caused global
OL,8,Fwarming and a supersized El Nino, a
OL,9,Fperiodic warming of parts of the
OL,10,FPacific that leads to temperature
OL,11,Fvariations around the globe, there's
OL,12,Fan increasing chance that by the end
OL,13,Fof the year, 2026 could become the
OL,14,Fhottest year on record, beating out
OL,15,F2024 ` or at least come close,
OL,16,Fscientists said.
OL,26,@pD@_Tw
