OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F319A1786425557
OL,3,CWorld's seas hit hottest July
OL,4,Ctemperature on record, scientists say
OL,6,FThe record-breaking rise in average
OL,7,Fsea surface temperature was partially
OL,8,Ffueled by developing El Nino
OL,9,Fconditions in the equatorial Pacific,
OL,10,Fthe service said.
OL,12,FThe new average record for July is
OL,13,F20.96 degrees Celsius (69.73 degrees
OL,14,FFahrenheit), which beat the 2023
OL,15,Frecord of 20.89 C (69.60 F).
OL,17,FHowever, last month's average surface
OL,18,Fair temperature globally was 16.90C
OL,19,F(62.42 F), making it only the joint
OL,20,Fsecond warmest July on record and tied
OL,21,Fwith July 2024, Copernicus reported.
OL,26,@pD@[TwzD@cOX
