PN,31907
SC,0007
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F319A1786425557
OL,3,CWorld's seas hit hottest July
OL,4,Ctemperature on record, scientists say
OL,6,FScientists say 2025 was particularly
OL,7,Fexceptional, with marine heatwave
OL,8,Fconditions persisting for more than
OL,9,Fthree-quarters of the year. Similar
OL,10,Fevents were also recorded in 2022 and
OL,11,F2023, while 2026 has once again seen
OL,12,Fsea temperatures significantly above
OL,13,Faverage.
OL,15,FAt the same time, cold marine
OL,16,Fconditions have become increasingly
OL,17,Frare. The last widespread cold spell
OL,18,Faffecting UK waters occurred during
OL,19,Fthe Beast from the East in 2018. Since
OL,20,Fthen, winters have tended to feature
OL,21,Fabove-average sea temperatures.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G7/8
